{"name":"Springtime","hex":"#e9e5b3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"springtime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The season of spring, between winter and summer.","A period of flourishing and renewal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/springtime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring (season)","blocks":[{"text":"Spring, also known as springtime, is one of the four temperate seasons, succeeding winter and preceding summer. There are various technical definitions of spring, but local usage of the term varies according to local climate, cultures and customs. When it is spring in the Northern Hemisphere, it is autumn in the Southern Hemisphere and vice versa. At the spring equinox, also called the vernal equinox, days and nights are approximately twelve hours long, with daytime length increasing and nighttime length decreasing as the season progresses until the summer solstice. The spring equinox is in March in the Northern Hemisphere and in September in the Southern Hemisphere, while the summer solstice is in June in the Northern Hemisphere and in December in the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg/330px-Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_(season)","wikidata":"Q1312"},{"title":"Springtime (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Springtime is a 1920 American silent comedy film directed by Jess Robbins and starring Oliver Hardy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Springtime_%28Vitagraph%2C_1920%29_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Springtime_%28Vitagraph%2C_1920%29_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springtime_(1920_film)","wikidata":"Q7581195"},{"title":"Springtime (Springtime album)","blocks":[{"text":"Springtime is the debut album from Australian supergroup Springtime, consisting of Gareth Liddiard, Chris Abrahams and Jim White. Recorded over 15 days at Liddiard's home studio in Nagambie, the largely-improvised album features lyrics from his uncle Ian Duhig, in addition to a Will Oldham cover and a reworking of a track by The Drones. It was released in Australia through TFS Records and in the US through Joyful Noise Recordings to largely positive reviews."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Springtime_-_Springtime.pg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springtime_(Springtime_album)","wikidata":"Q111953914"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/1280px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cherry blossoms flowering during springtime in Christchurch, New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg/500px-Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm